1
00:06:15,000 --> 00:06:21,000
While the world was falling apart, they were falling in love.

2
00:12:30,000 --> 00:12:36,000
Ali and Nino is a drama, romance film directed by Asif Kapadia.

3
00:18:45,000 --> 00:18:51,000
Muslim prince Ali and Georgian aristocrat Nino have grown
up in the Russian province of Azerbaijan.

4
00:25:00,000 --> 00:25:06,000
Their tragic love story sees the outbreak of the First World
War and the world’s struggle for Baku’s oil.

5
00:31:15,000 --> 00:31:21,000
Ultimately they must choose to fight for their
country’s independence or for each other.

6
00:37:30,000 --> 00:37:36,000
Ali Khan Shirvanshir, played by Adam Bakri.

7
00:43:45,000 --> 00:43:51,000
Nino Kipiani, played by María Valverde.

8
00:50:00,000 --> 00:50:06,000
Duchess Kipiani, played by Connie Nielsen.

9
00:56:15,000 --> 00:56:21,000
Duke Kipiani, played by Mandy Patinkin.

10
01:02:30,000 --> 01:02:36,000
Seyid Mustafa, played by Numan Acar.

11
01:08:45,000 --> 01:08:51,000
Malik Nakhararyan, played by Riccardo Scamarcio.

12
01:15:00,000 --> 01:15:06,000
Ali and Nino is a 2016 British-Azerbaijani war film, based on
Kurban Said's 1937 novel of the same name.

13
01:21:15,000 --> 01:21:21,000
The film is written by Christopher Hampton and directed by Asif Kapadia.

14
01:27:30,000 --> 01:27:36,000
It stars Maria Valverde and Adam Bakri.

15
01:33:45,000 --> 01:33:51,000
The tone is emotional.
